### storage

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-DS-BINARY-STORAGE-FS-1","category":"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"storage","spec_ref":"DS-BINARY-STORAGE-FS","spec_file":"document-store-binary-enhancement.smd","spec_says":"Default blob directory: /var/lib/composeio/blobs/","impl_has":"_db_dir is parent of the .db file; blobs subdirectory is relative to that. If COMPOSEIO_DOCSTORE_DB=/var/lib/composeio/docstore.db then blob_directory=/var/lib/composeio/blobs — matches. But if DB is elsewhere the blob root moves with it.","impl_file":"server.py","recommendation":"Spec and implementation agree when using the default path. Add a note to the spec clarifying that blob_directory is always co-located with the DB file, not a fixed path. No code change needed.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-DS-BINARY-STORAGE-META-1","category":"UNDERSPECIFIED_NOW_IMPLEMENTED","priority":"P3","area":"storage","spec_ref":"DS-BINARY-STORAGE-META","spec_file":"document-store-binary-enhancement.smd","spec_says":"Table created at startup alongside existing collection tables.","impl_has":"Table created inside _load_collections(), which is called from __init__. Correct. However, _load_collections() also excludes _binary_meta from the _collections_cache set, which is correct but not stated in the spec.","impl_file":"server.py","recommendation":"Informational only. Implementation is sound. No action needed.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

