### http_api

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-DS-BINARY-API-PUT-1","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P3","area":"http_api","spec_ref":"DS-BINARY-API-PUT","spec_file":"document-store-binary-enhancement.smd","spec_says":"Response body shows status/collection/doc_id/size_bytes/content_type. No HTTP status code specified in the spec text.","impl_has":"Returns HTTP 201 Created for all PUT operations (both JSON and binary paths). The spec response example implies 200 by omission but does not state it explicitly.","impl_file":"server.py","recommendation":"201 is semantically correct for a create/upsert. Update the spec to explicitly state HTTP 201. No code change needed.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-DS-BINARY-API-LIST-1","category":"IMPLEMENTED_NOT_SPECIFIED","priority":"P3","area":"http_api","spec_ref":"DS-BINARY-API-LIST","spec_file":"document-store-binary-enhancement.smd","spec_says":"GET /api/v1/collections/{collection} returns documents array with type markers.","impl_has":"The JSON document entries include only {id, type:json} — no size_bytes or content_type for JSON docs, which is consistent with spec. However, the spec does not address the case where a collection has no JSON table (binary-only collection). Implementation handles this via binary_collections() set difference in list_collections(), but list_docs() for a binary-only collection would return empty list rather than 404.","impl_file":"server.py","recommendation":"Informational. The binary-only collection case is handled gracefully. Consider adding a note to the spec.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-DS-BINARY-API-GET-1","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"http_api","spec_ref":"DS-BINARY-API-GET","spec_file":"document-store-binary-enhancement.smd","spec_says":"GET checks _binary_meta first; if binary record exists serve raw bytes with stored Content-Type; otherwise fall through to JSON lookup.","impl_has":"Implementation does binary-first check correctly. However: if the binary metadata row exists but the filesystem file is missing (os.path.exists check fails), get_binary() returns None and the handler falls through to the JSON lookup instead of returning a 404 or 500. This creates a silent data-loss scenario — a corrupt store (meta row present, file deleted) returns a JSON 404 rather than an error indicating the binary record is broken.","impl_file":"server.py","recommendation":"In DocumentStore.get_binary(), when meta is found but file is missing, log an error and return a sentinel (e.g., raise an exception or return a distinct value) so the handler can return HTTP 500 or 404 with an informative body. Add a compliance note in the spec for this edge case.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"area_summary","id":"summary-http_api","area":"http_api","total_gaps":3,"by_category":{"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH":2,"IMPLEMENTED_NOT_SPECIFIED":1},"by_priority":{"P2":1,"P3":2},"notes":"One substantive gap (P2): missing-file-but-metadata-present case is silently swallowed. Two minor informational gaps."}

### python_client

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-DS-BINARY-CLIENT-1","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"python_client","spec_ref":"DS-BINARY-CLIENT-METHODS","spec_file":"document-store-binary-enhancement.smd","spec_says":"put_binary(collection, doc_id, data, content_type) -> dict","impl_has":"Returns None on exception rather than raising. The return type annotation says -> dict but the implementation can return None. Callers doing result['status'] will get a TypeError with no indication of what failed beyond a logged message.","impl_file":"python/composeio/docstore.py","recommendation":"Either annotate as -> dict | None (and update spec) or raise on failure. Given the existing client methods all return None on error, the pattern is consistent — but the spec signature implies dict always. Align spec to dict | None or add explicit error handling contract.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-DS-BINARY-CLIENT-2","category":"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH","priority":"P2","area":"python_client","spec_ref":"DS-BINARY-CLIENT-METHODS","spec_file":"document-store-binary-enhancement.smd","spec_says":"get_binary(collection, doc_id) -> tuple[bytes, str]","impl_has":"Returns None on 404 or exception. Same return-type mismatch as put_binary. Additionally, the timeout is 30s for binary methods vs 5s for JSON methods — this is a reasonable implementation choice not covered in the spec.","impl_file":"python/composeio/docstore.py","recommendation":"Update spec signature to tuple[bytes, str] | None. The 30s timeout is appropriate for large files; add a note to the spec or docstring.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"gap","id":"gap-DS-BINARY-CLIENT-3","category":"IMPLEMENTED_NOT_SPECIFIED","priority":"P3","area":"python_client","spec_ref":"DS-BINARY-CLIENT-METHODS","spec_file":"document-store-binary-enhancement.smd","spec_says":"Spec lists put_binary and get_binary as the two methods to add. No mention of Content-Length header on upload.","impl_has":"put_binary() explicitly sets Content-Length header on the request. This is correct HTTP practice and ensures the server can use _read_body() reliably. urllib.request may also set it automatically, making this redundant but harmless.","impl_file":"python/composeio/docstore.py","recommendation":"Informational only. No action needed.","status":"open","delta":"NEW"}

{"type":"area_summary","id":"summary-python_client","area":"python_client","total_gaps":3,"by_category":{"SPEC_IMPL_MISMATCH":2,"IMPLEMENTED_NOT_SPECIFIED":1},"by_priority":{"P2":2,"P3":1},"notes":"Two P2 return-type mismatches between spec signatures and actual implementation behavior. These are documentation accuracy gaps, not functional bugs."}

