### Actionable Gaps Only

| ID | Priority | Area | Summary |
|----|----------|------|---------|
| gap-DS-BINARY-API-GET-1 | P2 | http_api | Metadata-present / file-missing case returns silent None, falls through to JSON 404 |
| gap-DS-BINARY-CLIENT-1 | P2 | python_client | put_binary() return type is dict | None; spec says dict |
| gap-DS-BINARY-CLIENT-2 | P2 | python_client | get_binary() return type is tuple | None; spec says tuple[bytes, str] |
| gap-DS-BINARY-API-PUT-1 | P3 | http_api | PUT returns HTTP 201; spec implies 200 by omission |
| gap-DS-BINARY-API-LIST-1 | P3 | http_api | Binary-only collection path undocumented in spec |
| gap-DS-BINARY-CLIENT-3 | P3 | python_client | Explicit Content-Length header on upload not in spec (harmless) |
| gap-DS-BINARY-STORAGE-FS-1 | P3 | storage | Blob dir tied to DB location, not fixed path — clarify in spec |
| gap-DS-BINARY-STORAGE-META-1 | P3 | storage | _binary_meta exclusion from collections_cache not documented |

### Gate Assessment

- P0 issues: 0 — no blockers
- P1 issues: 0 — no significant documentation accuracy issues
- P2 issues: 3 — the missing-file edge case and the two return-type mismatches should be addressed before the spec is marked production-ready
- P3 issues: 5 — informational; address at spec update time

### Top Recommendations

1. In server.py DocumentStore.get_binary(): when meta row exists but filesystem file is absent, return a distinct error value (or raise) so the HTTP handler can respond with 500/data-corruption rather than silently falling through to JSON lookup.
2. Update spec signatures for put_binary() and get_binary() to reflect dict | None and tuple[bytes, str] | None return types, consistent with the rest of the client's error contract.
3. Update spec section DS-BINARY-API-PUT to state HTTP 201 explicitly — the implementation is correct, the spec is ambiguous.

